      "title": "LIN Q3 Earnings Beat Estimates on Higher Americas Pricing & Volumes",
      "summary": "Linde plc (LIN) reported Q3 2026 adjusted EPS of $4.59, up 9% year-over-year and beating consensus estimates by 1.55%. Revenue grew 9% to $9.40 billion, driven by higher pricing and volume growth across all regions. The company raised its full-year 2026 adjusted EPS guidance to $17.82-$17.92 (8-9% growth), supported by a strong $10.8 billion project backlog. However, LIN carries a Zacks Rank #4 (Sell) rating.",
